          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z To identify satellites in the sky, look for any moving object in the sky that appears as a point of light with steady or flickering brightness and is moving very fast across the sky. You can see them with the naked eye or with binoculars."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.163,
            0.883,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z You may use mobile apps or websites that provide details of satellites visible in your location and when they will be passing above you in the sky."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.234,
            0.438,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A step further"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.273,
            0.262,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
